## {{lb|en|transitive}} To make enter a race.
##: {{ux|en|He '''ran''' his best horse in the Derby.}}
##: {{ux|en|We're '''running''' two cars in today's rally.}}
## {{lb|en|transitive}} To make stand in an election.
##: {{ux|en|The Green Party is '''running''' twenty candidates in this election.}}
# To exert continuous activity; to proceed.
#: {{ux|en|to '''run''' through life; to '''run''' in a circle}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To be [[present]]ed in the [[media]].
#: {{ux|en|The story will '''run''' on the 6-o'clock news.}}
#: {{ux|en|The latest Robin Williams movie is '''running''' at the Silver City theatre.}}
#: {{ux|en|Her picture '''ran''' on the front page of the newspaper.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[print]] or [[broadcast]] in the media.
#: {{ux|en|'''run''' a story; '''run''' an ad}}
