# To extend or persist, statically or dynamically, through space or time.
## {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[extend]] in [[space]] or through a [[range]] (often with a measure phrase).
##: {{ux|en|The border '''runs''' for 3000 miles.}}
##: {{ux|en|The leash '''runs''' along a wire.}}
##: {{ux|en|The grain of the wood '''runs''' to the right on this table.}}
##: {{ux|en|It '''ran''' in quality from excellent to substandard.}}
## {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[extend]] in [[time]], to [[last]], to [[continue]] (usually with a measure phrase).
##: {{ux|en|The sale will '''run''' for ten days.}}
##: {{ux|en|The contract '''runs''' through 2008.}}
##: {{ux|en|The meeting '''ran''' late.}}
##: {{ux|en|The book '''runs''' 655 pages.}}
##: {{ux|en|The speech '''runs''' as follows: …}}
## {{lb|en|transitive}} To make (something) extend in space.
##: {{ux|en|I need to '''run''' this wire along the wall.}}
## {{lb|en|intransitive}} Of a [[machine]], including computer [[program]]s, to be [[operate|operating]] or [[work]]ing normally.
##: {{ux|en|My car stopped '''running'''.}}
##: {{ux|en|That computer '''runs''' twenty-four hours a day.}}
##: {{ux|en|The buses don't '''run''' on Sundays.}}
## {{lb|en|transitive}} To make a machine [[operate]].
##: {{ux|en|It's full. You can '''run''' the dishwasher now.}}
##: {{ux|en|Don't '''run''' the engine so fast.}}
