#* {{quote-book|en|year=1886|translator=H.L. Br&aelig;kstad|author=w:Peter Christen Asbj&oslash;rnsen|title=Folk and Fairy Tales|page=309|passage="Just look here! I am a parson now. Here is both the gown and the '''ruff'''!"}}
#* {{RQ:Wodehouse Jeeves in the Offing|chapter=XII|passage="When we first forgathered, I was sitting on the floor with a chair round my neck." "Like an Elizabethan '''ruff''', as worn by Thomas Botway." "Otway," I said stiffly.}}
# Anything formed with [[plait#Noun|plaits]] or [[fluting#Noun|flutings]] like a frill.
