# {{non-gloss|Senses relating to animals.}}
## A [[gregarious]], [[medium-sized]] [[wading bird]] of species {{taxlink|Calidris pugnax|species}} (syn. {{taxfmt|Philomachus pugnax|species}}), of [[Eurasia]]; ''specifically'', a [[male]] of the [[species]] which develops a [[distinctive]] ruff of feathers and [[ear]] [[tuft]]s during [[mating season]] (the [[female]] is called a {{m|en|reeve|id=bird}}).
##* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Desmond Nethersole-Thompson; Maimie Nethersole-Thompson|chapter=New or Returning Waders|title=Waders: Their Breeding, Haunts and Watchers|location=Calton, Staffordshire|publisher=w:T. & A. D. Poyser|year=1986|isbn=978-0-85661-042-4|title2=Waders: Their Breeding, Haunts and Watchers|series2=Poyser Monographs|location2=London|publisher2=T. & A. D. Poyser|year2=2010|page2=323|pageurl2=https://books.google.com/books?id=ivvUBAAAQBAJ&pg=PA323|isbn2=978-1-4081-3747-5|passage=A reeve shows her readiness to copulate by crouching in a particular residence. In a crowded lek she selects an individual '''ruff''' by turning towards him while still crouching. Some '''ruffs''' are thus chosen frequently while others are never selected. '''Ruff''' and reeve only copulate after she has crouched and has sometimes nibbled the feathers at the back of the '''ruff'''’s head.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|author=Johan G. van Rhijn|chapter=The Vigilant Mother|title=The Ruff: Individuality in a Gregarious Wading Bird|location=London|publisher=w:T. & A. D. Poyser|year=1991|isbn=978-0-85661-062-2|title2=The Ruff: Individuality in a Gregarious Wading Bird|series2=Poyser Monographs|location2=London|publisher2=T. & A. D. Poyser|year2=2010|page2=111|pageurl2=https://books.google.com/books?id=9-yViWFSVS8C&pg=PA111|isbn2=978-1-4081-3678-2|passage=During late spring and early summer it becomes difficult to detect '''Ruffs''' in their breeding habitat. The males no longer visit the leks, and most have left the area. Some of the females may still be sitting on their eggs, invisible to casual passers-by.}}
## {{lb|en|ornithology}} A set of [[lengthened#Adjective|lengthened]] or otherwise [[modified#Adjective|modified]] [[feather#Noun|feathers]] on or around the [[neck#Noun|neck]] of a [[bird]].
