#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Zia Mahmood; David Burn|chapter=The Shriek|editor=Ray Lee|title=Around the World in 80 Hands|location=Toronto, Ont.|publisher=w:Master Point Press|year=1999|page=15|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=3X22r6Y2d3YC&pg=PA15|isbn=978-1-894154-08-6|passage=Then I played on diamonds, to '''ruff''' out the suit&nbsp;– but East had four diamonds and West none, so I had annoyingly to lose a trick to East's ♣K in the end.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Ken Casey|chapter=Introduction: Focus Your Attention on Ruffing Losers|chapterurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=USwyDAAAQBAJ&pg=PP11|title=Playing Beginning Bridge|location=[Bloomington, Ind.]|publisher=w:Xlibris|year=2016|isbn=978-1-5144-7992-6|passage=It never ceases to amaze me how many times people get in trouble by failing to first '''ruff''' out their sure losers.}}

