===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*ḱers-}}{{etymid|en|hurry}}
Perhaps from {{inh|en|enm|ruschen}}, {{m|enm|russchen|t=to rush, startle, make a loud rushing noise}}, from {{inh|en|ang|hrysċan|t=to jolt, startle}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*hurskijan}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*hurskijaną|t=to startle, drive}}, from {{m|gem-pro|*hurskaz|t=fast, rapid, quick}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*ḱers-|t=to run, hurry}}.

Cognate with {{cog|goh|hursken|t=to hurry, speed, incite, accelerate}}, {{cog|ang|horsċ|t=quick, quick-witted, clever}}, {{cog|ofs|rosk}}, {{m|ofs|rosch|t=quick, rapid, sudden}}.

{{col-top|2|etymology note}}
An alternative etymology traces ''rush'' via {{der|en|enm|ruschen|t=to rush}} from {{cog|ang|*rūscian|t=to rush}} from {{der|en|gem-pro|*rūskōną|t=to rush, storm, be fierce, be cruel}}, a variant (with formative ''k'') of {{der|en|gem-pro|*rūsōną|t=to be cruel, storm, rush}} from {{der|en|ine-pro|*(o)rewə-|t=to drive, move, agitate}}, making it akin to {{cog|goh|rosci|rosc, rosci|quick}}, {{cog|gml|rûschen|t=to rush}}, {{cog|gmh|ruschen|rūschen, riuschen|t=to rush}} ({{cog|de|rauschen|t=to rush}}), {{cog|frr|ruse|t=to rush}}, {{cog|dum|ruuscen|t=to make haste}}, {{cog|dum|rusen|rūsen|t=to rush}} ({{cog|nl|ruisen|t=to rush}}), {{cog|da|ruse|t=to rush}}, {{cog|sv|rusa|t=to rush}}. Compare {{cog|gmh|rūsch|t=a charge, rush}}. Influenced by {{der|en|enm|russhen|t=to force back}} from {{cog|xno|russer|russher, russer}} from {{cog|fro|ruser|ruser, rëuser}}.

Alternatively, according to the OED, perhaps an adaptation of {{der|en|xno|-}} {{m|fro|russher}}, {{m|fro|russer|t=to force back, down, out of place, by violent impact", "to pull out or drag off violently or hastily}}, from {{der|en|fro|rehusser|re(h)usser}}, {{m|fro|ruser}} (although the connection of the forms with single ''-s-'' and double ''-ss-'' is dubious; also adopted in English {{m|en|ruse}}; French {{m|fr|ruser|t=to retreat, drive back}}), from an assumed {{cog|la-vul|*refūsāre}} and Latin {{m|fro|refundō|t=I cause to flow back}}, although connection to the same {{der|en|gem}} root is also possible. More at {{m|en|rouse}}.
{{col-bottom}}

