From {{inh|en|enm|robe}}, {{m|enm|roobe}}, from {{der|en|fro|robe}}, {{m|fro|robbe}}, {{m|fro|reube|t=booty, spoils of war, robe, garment}}, from {{der|en|frk|*rouba}}, {{m|frk|*rauba|t=booty, spoils, stolen clothes|lit=things taken}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*raubō}}, {{m|gem-pro|*raubaz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*raubą|t=booty, that which is stripped or carried away}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*Hrewp-|t=to tear, peel}}.
{{col-top|2|cognates and related terms}}
Akin to {{cog|goh|roup|t=booty}} (Modern {{cog|de|Raub|t=robbery, spoils}}), {{cog|goh|roubōn|t=to rob, steal}} (Modern {{cog|de|rauben|t=to rob}}), {{cog|ang|rēaf|t=spoils, booty, dress, armour, robe, garment}}, {{cog|ang|rēafian|t=to steal, deprive}}. Cognate with {{cog|es|ropa|t=clothing, clothes}}. More at [[rob]], [[reaf]], [[reave]].
